		{
			dependencies: ["4F4F4D2EB4A0F184"]
			description: [
				"The Varasuchus is a highly adaptive semi-aquatic dragon species known for its phase-shifting combat behavior and deceptive threat presentation. Varasuchus individuals initially appear restrained and energy-efficient, often displaying limited aggression during early encounters. Varasuchus relies heavily on delayed escalation. Sustained threats trigger a drastic physiological transition in posture, musculature, and combat behavior, shifting the species from a quadrupedal stance into a far more aggressive bipedal combat phase. This transformation is not believed to be emotional, but tactical. Once escalation occurs, Varasuchus abandons passive territorial tolerance entirely and engages targets with calculated, sustained aggression. Early civilizations frequently utilized domesticated Varasuchus due to their aquatic mobility and defensive potential. In their quadrupedal state, most individuals exhibit measured aggression and relatively stable behavior, leading many settlements to integrate them into fishing operations, shoreline protection, and transport across difficult terrain. When met in the wild, they are typically neutral."
				"Unlike many dragon species, &4&nVarasuchus are not subdued through direct combat&r. Instead, taming &4&nrequires the rider to remain mounted long enough to exhaust and destabilize the dragon's resistance&r. Wild Varasuchus will violently attempt to throw riders off during the process, &n&4requiring repeated mounting attempts before successful domestication can occur&r."
				""
				"{image:tumblrbumblr:textures/quests/varasuchus.png width:300 height:169 align:center}"
			]
			id: "7EFAB0353D571EF1"
			rewards: [
				{
					amount: 70L
					currency: "eternalcurrencies:ancientcoins"
					id: "1853CFE535C0851D"
